  "name": "CHRONIC NEUTROPHILIC LEUKEMIA (CNL)(CSF3R GENE - EXON 14 & 17; SETBP GENE - EXON 4)",
  "code": "2303",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"819\" data-end=\"967\">\n<p data-start=\"821\" data-end=\"967\"><strong data-start=\"821\" data-end=\"845\">CSF3R T618I Mutation</strong>: A pathogenic mutation commonly associated with Chronic Neutrophilic Leukemia (CNL). Its presence supports the diagnosis.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"968\" data-end=\"1088\">\n<p data-start=\"970\" data-end=\"1088\"><strong data-start=\"970\" data-end=\"990\">SETBP1 Mutations</strong>: Frequently seen in myeloid malignancies, associated with poor prognosis and disease progression.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1089\" data-end=\"1233\">\n<p data-start=\"1091\" data-end=\"1233\">If <strong data-start=\"1094\" data-end=\"1123\">no mutations are detected</strong>, clinical correlation and cytogenetic studies are recommended to rule out other myeloproliferative disorders.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
  "showInterpretation": false,
  "sampleType": "edta wb",
  "department": "6414fd22f02dc1ebb6a097ef",
